  "id": "biological-measures",
  "term": "biological measures",
  "definition": "Biological measures are bodily indicators used to assess stress by tracking activity in stress-response systems. In research on children’s daily stress, these measures most often include endocrine markers such as cortisol and autonomic nervous system indicators, with brain- and immune-related markers used less often.",
